<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Two wheats in one colony.

    Mlie's Vanilla-like Wheat (Continued) is a common mod, and it grows wheat too: PlantWheat,
    labelled "wheat plant", harvested as RawWheat. Nothing collides - the defNames differ - but a
    growing zone offering two entries called "wheat plant", one of them needing research and a
    quern and the other not, is a nuisance rather than a choice.

    So when that mod is loaded, this one stands down: FZPlant_Wheat loses its sowTags and drops
    out of the sow menu, and the fifteen recipes take Mlie's RawWheat instead - they already
    accept it, through MayRequire in Recipes_FZfood_Meals.xml.

    The test is on the def, not on the mod. PatchOperationFindMod would have been the obvious
    tool, but it matches on ModMetaData.Name by exact string equality - "Vanilla-like wheat
    (Continued)", capital letters and parentheses included - and that name is Mlie's to change.
    PlantWheat is what actually causes the problem, so PlantWheat is what is tested.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="PlantWheat"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="FZPlant_Wheat"]/plant/sowTags</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
